(:room
 :id "tea-table"
 :title "Lawn and Tea Table"
 :body
 ((:p "The motor turns in at the lodge gates and the old house comes into view. Before tea, John introduces you to Evelyn Howard in the garden: blunt, sunburnt, vigorous. \"If you mean to be useful at Styles, Captain Hastings, keep your eyes open and your mouth shut,\" she says.")
  (:p "She leads you round the house to the lawn, where tea is laid under a wide tree. Mary Cavendish rises from a basket chair with a stillness that catches you off guard; Emily Inglethorp presides kindly but completely; Alfred hovers near her; Cynthia comes bright from hospital work; Evelyn watches Alfred with open contempt.")
  (:p "You are still only a guest, but the household has begun arranging itself before you like evidence: old affection, new marriage, money, dependence, charm, resentment, and a politeness too thin to hide the cracks.")
  (:when (:marked? :clue-evie-warning)
   (:p "Evelyn's warning hangs in the air: \"That man is dangerous.\" It was blunt enough to seem honest."))
  (:when (:marked? :clue-cynthia-dispensary)
   (:p "Cynthia's dispensary work gives her brightness a sharper edge: she handles medicines every day."))
  (:once
   :id :styles-ask-evelyn
   (:choice
    "Ask Evelyn why she distrusts Alfred"
    ((:mark :clue-evie-warning)
     (:say "\"Because he is a dangerous man,\" Evelyn says. \"Look at him with Mrs. Inglethorp, Mr. Hastings, and tell me I am wrong if you dare.\""))))
  (:once
   :id :styles-ask-cynthia-tea
   (:choice
    "Ask Cynthia about the dispensary"
    ((:mark :clue-cynthia-dispensary)
     (:say "\"Oh, we are tremendously scientific at the dispensary,\" Cynthia says, laughing. \"Bromides, strychnine, bottles with skulls on them. Enough to make one quite important.\" The names come easily to her."))))
  (:once
   :id :styles-ask-mary-poisons
   (:choice
    "Ask Mary about poisons"
    ((:mark :clue-mary-poison-talk)
     (:say "\"Poisons are rather fascinating, are they not?\" Mary says lightly. Then her eyes meet yours. \"You look shocked, Captain Hastings. I promise I am only being idle.\""))))
  (:choice "Retire for the night" (:go "night-crisis"))))
